Yes, there are the same issues that concern the idea of portable bones and
save files that has been mentioned every now and then:
What should the game do if the imported file contains something that isn't
compiled in the game that loads the file? One possibility would be to
totally ignore the unsupported thing, another would be to replace it with
something else close enough that IS supported. In the latter case, there
should be some pointer in the optional / additional item structure that
would tell what it can be replaced with. 
Like, if some patch adds a monster "lion", it could contain information
that directs an unpatched game to replace it with a tiger.
And the vacuum cleaner could be replaced with a bag of holding or a sack
in an unpatched game.

